    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L08-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "8.4: Missing Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes we know the value of an exponential expression but we don’t know the exponent that produces that value.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l08.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L08-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "8.4: Missing Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, suppose the population of a town was 1 thousand. Since then, the population has doubled every decade and is currently at 32 thousand. How many decades has it been since the population was 1 thousand?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l08.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L08-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "8.4: Missing Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If we say that \\(d\\) is the number of decades since the population was 1 thousand, then \\(1 \\boldcdot 2^d\\), or just \\(2^d\\), represents the population, in thousands, after \\(d\\) decades. To answer the question, we need to find the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l08.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L08-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "8.4: Missing Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When did the town have 250 people? Assuming that the doubling started before the population was measured to be 1 thousand, we can write: \\(2^d = 0.25\\) or \\(2^d = \\frac14\\). We know that \\(2^{\\text-2}=\\frac14\\), so the exponent \\(d\\) has a…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l08.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L08-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "8.4: Missing Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "But it may not always be so straightforward to calculate. For example, it is harder to tell the value of \\(d\\) in \\(2^d = 805\\) or in \\(2^d = 4.5\\). In upcoming lessons, we’ll learn more ways to find unknown exponents.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l08.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
